 (`build_class_move_edit`).
+
+
+## F24. Preserve unresolved hierarchy target alternatives
+
+**Impact: Medium · Complexity: High**
+
+The Workbench call hierarchy extension accounts for inspected invocation sites.
+A known edge at a call site can still mask an unresolved receiver alternative
+when an ordinary member or literal array target has several possible types.
+Expose completeness through the shared callable resolver, retain all known
+edges, and report the original call site as partial when any alternative cannot
+be resolved. Cover missing and magic methods, branch unions and selectors
+without introducing a second type-resolution path.
+
+## F25. Account for unavailable workspace hierarchy sources
+
+**Impact: Medium · Complexity: Medium-High**
+
+Incoming hierarchy coverage currently inspects published user symbol maps.
+A workspace file skipped before map publication, such as an unreadable or
+non-UTF8 source, is outside that inventory. Retain indexing admission/failure
+receipts so hierarchy can distinguish excluded files from unavailable source,
+then report partial workspace coverage without reading excluded files or
+inventing caller nodes. The invocation coverage budget bounds analysis after
+index construction; whole-file parsing and legacy edge resolution still need
+independent performance/resource acceptance.
